viewers will never see your home feed. They'll never know you watch UPSC drama.\n\n### Now, your real question: Edit the old channel or create new?\n\n**Edit the old channel. It's fine.** Here's why:\n\n- Zero uploads = zero creator signals = blank slate. YouTube's creator algorithm has literally nothing on this channel. It's empty.\n- Changing name + logo + description = the same as creating fresh, because there ARE no signals to contaminate\n- Phone verification already done\n- One less thing to manage\n\n**The ONLY reason to create a new Brand Channel would be if:**\n- The old channel had uploads (it doesn't)\n- The old channel had subscribers (doubtful with zero videos)\n- You plan to use the old channel for Nishchay Stories later\n\nIf you're abandoning Nishchay Stories completely → edit the old channel, change everything, start uploading audiobooks.\n\nIf you MIGHT want Nishchay Stories later → create a Brand Channel (takes 2 minutes, same Gmail, keeps old channel intact).\n\n### About the home feed \"contamination\"\n\nAfter you upload 3-5 audiobook videos and start watching audiobook content yourself, your home feed will shift within a week. YouTube re-learns fast. You can also:\n- Click \"Not Interested\" on the UPSC/drama recommendations\n- Go to `History → Manage all history → Delete` to clear old watch history\n- Subscribe to audiobook channels\n\nBut again — **none of this affects your creator channel.** This is just to clean up YOUR personal feed so it stops annoying you.\n\n### Bottom line\n\n**Edit the old channel.** Change name, logo, banner, description. Start uploading. Your home feed is irrelevant to your channel's performance. Don't overthink this — it's a 0-upload channel with nothing on it. There's nothing to contaminate.","thinking":"I see the screenshot. His YouTube home feed is completely filled with UPSC, IAS, Hindi drama, storytelling content — Stories Vibe, Rajasthani Rasiya World, Shuaib Tales. The topic pills show \"Union Public Service Commission\", \"Hindi drama plots\", \"Pakistani drama snippets\", \"Indian thriller series\", etc.\n\nThis is his personal YouTube home feed, which is completely trained on Hindi drama/stories content (Nishchay Stories niche). He's worried that if he creates a channel on this same account, the recommendations going to his viewers will be contaminated.\n\nLet me be real with him:\n\n**Key distinction he's missing:** His PERSONAL home feed (what YouTube recommends to HIM as a viewer) has NOTHING to do with his CREATOR channel's algorithmic identity. \n\nHis personal feed is driven by his own watch history, while what gets recommended to viewers of his content depends on his uploads, titles, and audience — these are separate systems, so the messy home feed is irrelevant to his new channel's performance. Now I'm weighing whether he should edit the existing Nishchay Stories channel or start a new Brand Channel, thinking through the tradeoffs of reusing the verified channel versus the risk if it already has uploads and watch history tied to it.\n\nSince he mentioned the channel has zero uploads, subscribers, or community posts, there's essentially no creator-side algorithmic baggage — it's a blank slate, so editing the name, logo, and description directly should be perfectly fine rather than creating a brand new channel from scratch.\n\nWatch history doesn't influence how YouTube recommends a creator's videos to others, so it's not a factor here. The real answer is simple: with zero uploads and zero subscribers, the existing channel is already a blank slate, so editing it is just as good as creating new — and phone verification is already done, making a new channel pointless."}
